{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Main Event Loop.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Main Event Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender main event loop blender main event loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Main Event Loop.md","fileName":"Blender Main Event Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Main Event Loop","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Core Source Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Core Source Architecture","Blender bContext Structure","Blender GHOST Event Pump","Blender Event Distribution Pipeline","Blender Model-View Update Order","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Main Event Loop.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Main Event Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender main event loop blender main event loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Main Event Loop.md","fileName":"Blender Main Event Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Main Event Loop","heading":"Blender Main Event Loop","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`WM_main()` is Blender's continuously running application loop. Each pass obtains and dispatches operating-system events, processes the window and editor handlers that respond to them, handles deferred notifiers, and then updates drawing.\n\nThe loop passes a [[Blender bContext Structure]] through each high-level stage so the same current application state remains available. Low-level input arrives through the [[Blender GHOST Event Pump]], becomes Blender-specific work in the [[Blender Event Distribution Pipeline]], and ends with the [[Blender Model-View Update Order]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Core Source Architecture","Blender bContext S